The claim 'Attempts have been made to develop **something** for constructing SPARQL queries.' is supported by the citation.
<accept> The content explicitly states that "Significant work has already been done to facilitate domain users and working biologist to either formulate complex queries using user interfaces [7, 8] or with the help of visualisations [9, 10]". It also mentions "man-made services designed to help researcher to access, search and query relevant RDF database" and that "AI bots" and "Generative AI tools" are being used and explored for "generating federated SPARQL queries" and "formulating simple and complex federated SPARQL queries". </accept>

**********Source Check**********

The claim 'Possible future directions in the field also include the potential use of AI chatbots to **in a certain way**.' is supported by the citation.
<accept> The conclusion section discusses "future directions" for AI chatbots. It states that "AI chatbots can be trained and fine-tuned to generate better results suited for specific needs," indicating a future way they can be used. It also mentions that "Filtering methods based on confidence levels in language models may be explored" to address limitations, which is another potential future way AI chatbots could be utilized or integrated into systems. These statements collectively support the idea of potential future uses of AI chatbots in "certain ways." </accept>

